<title>USA: U.S. copper rod inventories up in May - ABMS.</title>
<headline>U.S. copper rod inventories up in May - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total copper inventories at U.S. rod mills (including cathodes, scrap, rod and in-process material) rose by the end of May to 132,920,000 lbs from an April total of 120,281,000 lbs, American Bureau of Metal Statistics said.</p>
<p>Rod production fell to 378,215,000 lbs from a revised total of 394,162,000 lbs in April. Receipts totaled 398,822,000 lbs in May down from April's revised total of 404,569,000 lbs.</p>
<p>Total shipments fell to 384,930,000 lbs in May from 407,413,000 lbs the previous month.</p>
<p>--New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1640</p>
</text>
